@startuml sequence-restoration-ingest
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: the automatic path of one book. The operator (or the nightly beat)
'       imports a source; worker-io maps the TIFF tree to books; each book runs
'       as a Celery chain (stage → clean pages → layout → OCR → math → render),
'       fanned out per page where it pays. Every finished page is an event on
'       Redis pub/sub that the API streams to the SPA (SSE), so progress bars
'       move live. A quality gate ends the chain: clean books publish on their
'       own, flagged books land in the review queue (sequence-restoration-review).
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one book of an import, proposal. Scope: the job
'       and event flow. Omitted: retries/back-off details, telemetry spans,
'       metadata lookup (OPAC), cover generation, archival PDF/A validation.
' Source: design session 2026-11-07 (Celery + shared redis, CPU-only AI with
'         on-demand VLM, review only when flagged); evilflowers-books-digitalizer
'         pipeline (steps scantailor, ocr, render, reflow) and docs/reflow_edition.md
'         (VLM guards, worker recycling), 2026-11-07.
' Render: python3 tools/diagrams/render.py vault/evilflowers-knowledge/Diagrams/sequence-restoration-ingest.puml
' =============================================================================

title One book, imported and processed automatically, progress streamed (proposal, 2026-11-07)

actor "**Operator**\nSPA (VPN)" as op
participant "**studio-api**\nFastAPI" as api <<focus>>
database "**postgresql18**\ndb digitalizer" as pg
queue "**redis**\nCelery db 8 · pub/sub" as redis
participant "**worker-io**" as wio
participant "**worker-cpu**" as wcpu
participant "**worker-ai**" as wai
participant "**NFS** · gateway\nraw-scans ro · digitized rw" as nfs
participant "**vlm** :8000\nPaddleOCR-VL (TBC)" as vlm

op -> api : POST /projects/stu/imports\n{source: fei}
api -> pg : insert import (pending)
api -> redis : enqueue discover (queue io)
api --> op : 202 + import id
op -> api : GET /events?import=… (SSE, stays open)

redis -> wio : discover
wio -> nfs : list fei/FEI-skeny/*/stream_pages_tif
wio -> pg : upsert books + frames (queued)
wio -> redis : publish book.queued ×N
redis --> api : event
api --> op : SSE book.queued (board fills)

loop each book (queue io → cpu → ai, chained)
  redis -> wcpu : stage + clean (per frame group)
  wcpu -> nfs : read TIFF frames
  wcpu -> nfs : write cleaned pages + tiles
  wcpu -> redis : publish page.cleaned
  redis --> api : event
  api -[$accent_msg()]-> op : <b>SSE progress (page k / n)</b>
  redis -> wai : layout (per page, ONNX model in the image)
  wai -> pg : regions: kind · bbox · confidence\n(text, table, figure, formula, stamp…)
  redis -> wcpu : OCR + reflow analysis
  wcpu -> pg : words, disputes (low confidence,\nYOLO vs heuristics disagree)
  opt formulas within the CPU budget
    wai -> vlm : formula crops (HTTP)
    vlm --> wai : LaTeX (guards: hallucination,\nanchoring, MathML validation)
  end
  redis -> wcpu : render: distribution PDF · PDF/A-2b · EPUB
  wcpu -> nfs : write digitized/studio/<project>/<item_id>/…
  wcpu -> pg : quality report (scores, flags)
  alt all quality signals pass
    wcpu -> redis : enqueue publish (queue io)
    wcpu -> redis : publish book.ready
  else any flag (disputed regions, low OCR, rejected VLM)
    wcpu -> pg : book.status = review
    wcpu -> redis : publish book.review_needed
  end
  redis --> api : event
  api --> op : SSE book.ready / book.review_needed
end

caption Every arrow from redis is a Celery task delivery; every publish is a pub/sub event the API turns into a Server-Sent Event,\nso the board updates without polling. Per-page fan-out keeps one slow page from blocking a book; the VLM only sees formula\ncrops within the CPU budget. A clean book publishes on its own; a flagged book waits for an operator.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-knowledge · Diagrams/sequence-restoration-ingest.puml
@enduml
